{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implemented and pushed. Measured evidence for the false pass this ticket describes, using a wrapper mutated to launch nothing (`wrap()` returns /usr/bin/true):\n\n- OLD tests: 3 of the 4 enforcement tests PASSED, including test_the_incident_shape_rm_rf_is_denied. Only test_write_inside_the_allow_list_succeeds failed, because it alone was inherently self-proving. So the denial tests reported success while the sandbox did nothing at all.\n- NEW tests, same broken wrapper: all 4 FAIL with 'the child never reached its write, so a denied/absent target proves nothing'.\n\nLiveness comes from an artifact the CHILD wrote after starting (a sentinel in the allow-list), asserted before the denial is read. Exit status is explicitly not used, since a sandbox that fails to launch also exits non-zero.\n\nBlast radius: denial is now proven with a create wherever possible. Only the incident-shape test removes anything, and it carries three independent bounds — Python asserts the target is strictly inside tmp_path; the path reaches the shell only as \"${TARGET:?}\" so an empty value aborts instead of globbing from the root; and the sandbox denies the unlink. The ${VAR:?} guard test contains NO destructive command: it asserts the shell never reaches a marker, because proving the guard by really running rm on an empty variable would perform the incident whenever the guard stopped working.\n\nRED proofs (all by real mutation): wrapper launching nothing -> 18 failed; unguarded $TARGET -> guard test failed; containment check disabled -> escape test failed. Gate classes: 1871 passed, 4 skipped."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787880805044998001,"uuid":"ece70bd2-18d6-43b1-aeb2-f824a8247e34"}